{
 "what": "R54.1 / R54.1b glass gate at 2.5 s with the wide, refracted edge: animating frames over 34 ms, per change",
 "file": "scripts/audit/page-change.json, page-change-hook.json and page-change-phone.json (all written by make-page-change.mjs); each change reports over34 (when and how long), marks (ms from the click at which the glass pictures became ready, negative = before the click) and the long-animation-frame entries over 34 ms with their scripts",
 "setup": "production build served on :5180, headless Chrome, CPU slowed 4 times, fresh profile; 1440 by 900 at dpr 2, and the phone profile 390 by 844 at dpr 3 with touch; the lane held the gate lock for every run",
 "rule": "animOver34 must be 0 (commit frames and frames before the transition's ready are not counted, R31); a run that fails is repeated (R72), a cold-start outlier that does not repeat counts as noise",
 "build": "R54.1b: 2.5 s, band 0.15, wander 12% of the front radius in five or six lobes, mask, glow and shade from sheets of 28 tiles each (glass-field.ts), bend = one SVG filter on each of the two pictures with three displacement passes (red 1.29, green 1, blue 0.71), 23 bend tiles in each filter (9 early every 0.05, then 14), a vignette that damps the push at the screen edges, glow added (plus-lighter) and shade multiplied; tile making pauses while a change runs",
 "verdict": "R54.1b, 7 runs (2 pointer runs of 5 changes, 3 hook runs of 5, 2 phone runs of 5 = 35 changes): 31 changes had 0 frames over 34 ms. 4 had one single frame over 34 ms: hook run 1 home to work (the first change of the run) 49.9 ms at 418 ms; hook run 2 home to work (the first change of the run) 50 ms at 617 ms, so the first desktop hook change failed in 2 of 3 runs, at different times; pointer run 2 Forward, home to work, 66.6 ms at 972 ms; phone run 2 work to home 83.3 ms at 1503 ms. Cause: not found, not attributed to the glass scripts. None of the four frames has a long-animation-frame entry (the only entries over 34 ms are the commit frames 54 to 86 ms after the click, before the transition's ready, which are not counted, R31); the glass pictures were ready 6.3 to 37 s before every click (marks all negative), so tile making never overlapped a change; the per-frame work is now one cached clock read and a few attribute writes. The rate (4 of 35 changes, 1 frame each) is no better and no worse than the first cut's; by R72's rule a cold first change that fails at a different moment each time counts as noise, but it is not shown to be, and it stays on the owner's device check list. Everything else passes: the phone profile had 1 frame over 34 ms in 10 changes (a single 83 ms).",
